WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.170
- She is a four time
Grammy winner who sold

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.200
over 40 million records
and that's just on her own.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.810
Okay, she sold another 60 million

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.850
with a little group
called Destiny's Child.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.130
Never heard of them.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.070
Her latest EP is called
K, it's out right now.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.360
Let's say hi to Kelly Rowland everybody!

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.919
(slow jazz music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:24.550
Oh every time I see you,
you're like a glowing kind

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.230
of beautiful, it's annoying Kelly.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.240
It's-

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.997
(giggling)

00:00:29.997 --> 00:00:31.437
I like literally every time
I see you, I'm just like

00:00:31.437 --> 00:00:32.900
"How does she glow?

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:33.850
Like always."

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.840
- You are so sweet, but I'm telling you,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.910
it's the makeup girl, you know how we do?

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.350
- Oh, I, I have a whole team,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.550
I call them Harry Potter collectively.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.560
So momma didn't look like this.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.060
Do you and your husband
ever prank each other?

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.230
- You know what?

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.270
He has pranked me, when
we first started dating.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.470
I remember at my place in Miami

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.440
when I lived there years ago,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.460
when it was dark outside
'cause I lived like, you know

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.670
on the beach and it was super super dark.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.150
So I would go to one
room like in the kitchen

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.110
and he would cut off every single light

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.590
in the rest of the house.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.670
And he knew that I'm
like freakishly sometimes

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.920
like scared of the dark
specifically in that place.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.260
I've grown out of it now, but all my,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.220
and he would click off
one light at a time.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.100
So it was just some spooky,
weird, crazy Freddy stuff.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.310
I was like, this is so mean.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.920
But yeah, he pranks me all the time,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.820
I just need to get him back better.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.360
- Yeah, I don't do pranks on people

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.110
'cause I don't like people
do pranks on me, nope.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.810
Well, when you were on
this show last year,

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.450
you talked about wanting another baby.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.320
So, you know be careful what you wish for

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.270
'cause you got one.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.480
- That's so fast.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.870
I mean, it's funny.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.680
I can't, I can't believe how it happened

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.710
but it was just so, so crazy
how fast that turnaround was.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.509
And I wonder if like shortly after,

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:54.790
I should have to actually
take a note of that.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.920
I should have probably seen

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.110
if I was pregnant when
I talked to you huh?

00:01:59.110 --> 00:01:59.970
- I mean, I don't know.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:00.980
Yeah, that's it.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.690
I can't not talk about
that photo we just saw,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.810
isn't that the sweetest thing

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.510
'cause my kids are like
a couple years apart.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.580
When you see the older one just hovering

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.230
over the little baby one.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.030
Oh, it's my favorite.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.860
- Titan is obsessed with
Noah to the umpteenth power.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.620
Like as soon as he comes home from school

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.230
like him wanting to like,
if he hears him just

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.817
whimper, "Noah, Noah",

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.840
like he's his everything.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.970
So I think he feels like that's his baby.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.820
- I mean, I know his face in that picture.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.400
It's just so much joy and like pride

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.470
and he's not even the
dad it's like, but you

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.890
you posted this video of your
son, let's see it real quick.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.930
- Whoa, I'm Steve Irwin.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.773
Look at me.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.080
Let me show you some snakes.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.670
This boom snake is highly venomous.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:58.670
These camouflage themselves
like grand wine snakes.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.183
The camouflages are completely good.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.100
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.130
He is so freaking cute.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.493
Is he training to hunt crocodile some day?

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.840
- Girl, he absolutely loves snakes,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.180
loves alligators, everything.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.140
And I showed him one
YouTube of Steve Irwin

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.710
and now he wants to watch
Steve Irwin all day and night.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.590
He thinks he's the coolest person,

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.840
he's obsessed with Steve Irwin.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.770
- So congratulations on the new EP.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.410
You've been working on these
songs for quite a while, right?

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.470
- [Kelly Rowland] Yes I have.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.930
- So why not, so why now?

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.280
Why did it finally come to fruition now?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.570
- You know what?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.300
For me Kellz, I feel like, I didn't

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.700
I didn't have the worry about a label.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.640
You know what I mean?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.560
And for me, I just really wanted
to create from a free place

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.680
and I, and I did and it was awesome.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.050
And not to say that I
couldn't before, it's just

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.930
a different kind of space
and it just felt amazing.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.270
And I'm happy that I did.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.150
I'm happy that I released it.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.160
And to be honest, like really
honest, like it's so strange

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.800
like releasing music in
this, in this time and space

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.290
compared to the time
where we released music,

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.123
you know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:04:13.123 --> 00:04:15.230
- Everything's so
different wouldn't you say?

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.600
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.980
I don't know what the hell's happening.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:18.990
I just said, "Here it is.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.520
And you do whatever you're
supposed to do with it."

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.900
Like, yeah, it's so different.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.300
And I feel like in our careers especially,

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.610
like just in that amount of
time, things are so different.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.020
How we, how we buy music,

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.940
how we re you know, listen to music.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.193
There's been so many different platforms.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.350
- It's so different.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.430
And I was saying that to someone else,

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.310
I said, you know, as everybody

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.452
like digest music so much quicker now

00:04:41.452 --> 00:04:44.010
so it's not like a whole set up process.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.810
Like, and I love the
way this new generation

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.010
just releasing music.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.130
Like when they feel something,

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.550
they put it out and I'm
like, I'm good with that,

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.140
I'm gonna try that and see what happens.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.211
- I love that.

00:04:53.211 --> 00:04:55.940
Is it true that you took
over your husband's man-cave

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.920
to record this album?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.130
- Yes, I took over my husband's man cave.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.142
Just, I mean, we're in here now.

00:05:02.142 --> 00:05:04.920
(laughing)

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.422
- How does he feel about this?

00:05:07.422 --> 00:05:09.560
- I'm like, it's just such a vibe in here.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.680
He's got these cool
black and white pictures

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.280
and like this nice screen on the wall.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.727
It's just a vibe in here and he's like,

00:05:15.727 --> 00:05:17.770
"Am I gonna ever see my cave again?"

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.970
I was like, "Hoo maybe."

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.310
- And now you can just call it you know,

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:25.723
an adult cave, it's just for
y'all don't let the kids in.

00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:26.673
- Exactly, exactly.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.490
- Well, I know that a very emotional song

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.700
on the record is called "Flowers".

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.510
So what's the story behind that one?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.610
- So "Flowers" happened, I heard it

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.630
and it just took over in emotion for me.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.180
Of course, it's about a
relationship and making sure

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.580
that you have this
beautiful give and take of

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.220
of love and affection
and not taking advantage

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.840
of the love that is there, that exists.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.090
But it made me think of my mother.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:52.923
You know what I mean?

00:05:52.923 --> 00:05:56.180
And all the things that I
may be wanted to tell her,

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:01.180
I should have told her
and just reminding myself,

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.700
it reminded me to really
not take advantage

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.830
of the people around me and
the relationships around me.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.240
And when you're able to
look at people in the eye

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.820
or pick up the phone to call them, like,

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.610
those are moments like,

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.340
you know, when they pass
on, you can't get back.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.920
I remember my first
birthday without my mom,

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.482
like I literally picked up the phone.

00:06:20.482 --> 00:06:21.800
I was like, "Why hasn't my mom?"

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.360
And I just froze and I
was like, "Oh my God."

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.260
And I called Lala instead, my best friend.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.410
And she was like, "It's all right",

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.800
she was like, "Just talk
to her, she's right there."

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.030
And literally I did.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:32.863
And when I talked to her,

00:06:32.863 --> 00:06:36.500
the conversation just
continued, continued, continued.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.400
So I do feel like she's
here spiritually, but you

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.330
you just wanna give people their flowers

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.440
while they're here, while
they can smell them.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.850
And they mean so much to you.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:46.320
This is so important.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.630
So you know "Flowers" is just me loving

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.660
on everybody else that listens to it.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:51.963
- I love that.

00:06:51.963 --> 00:06:55.270
It's, it's been 15 years
since Destiny's child ended.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.900
And that was, it's just,
you're like the most

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.120
famous girl group ever,
like, was that, so that,

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.290
how crazy is it that that was your start?

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.540
And then now you've had such
a huge career after that.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.300
Like not many people are blessed

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.730
with that kind of longevity.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.160
Do you just feel massively
blessed because of that?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.990
'Cause that's an, it's a
crazy amount of success.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.100
- Kel, Kelly this is so crazy

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.700
that we're having this conversation.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.420
I promise you the day before yesterday,

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:24.040
Michelle called me and we
know each other very well

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:28.040
but I just had this like great like weep,

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.163
because I felt so incredibly
blessed that it scared me.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:33.843
- [Clarkson] Yeah.

00:07:33.843 --> 00:07:34.676
- It scared me.

00:07:34.676 --> 00:07:37.587
I know that sounds really
insane but I was like,

00:07:37.587 --> 00:07:39.050
"Oh Lord, I'm so grateful for this.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:39.990
And I'm so grateful for that.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.460
And my family is healthy and this",

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.060
like it was so many different things

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.300
and I felt so overwhelmed with gratitude

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.270
that it just kind of erupted.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.780
And Michelle's like,
"What'd you mad about?"

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.210
My eyes were dry, she was
like, "You can't fool me,

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.740
you got glassy eyes girl, what happened?"

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.080
And so I just told her

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.830
and we just kind of like
had this moment, like

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.290
'cause I said, you know

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.810
I could literally be
twiddling my fingers right now

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:06.910
wondering what's going to
happen, you know, next.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.870
And we're all doing that, you know?

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:10.580
And we were all doing
that at one point in time.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:15.533
But like, I'm kept, my family
is safe, we are healthy.

00:08:15.533 --> 00:08:17.940
It's I don't have to
complain about anything.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.360
I don't feel the need to
complain about anything.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.160
And I just am grateful for that.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.800
I think that we have to
remain humble, especially now.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:31.070
Like, you know, no matter how
high the heights you've seen,

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.200
you still keep your feet on the ground.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.120
'Cause it's the sweetest spot to stay in,

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.270
you know where you are

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.120
and you can still enjoy the heights

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.370
of wherever God wants
to take you but yeah,

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.580
I'm so grateful.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.610
- I agree.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.900
I always consider everything I
tell my friends and my family

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:47.733
I'm like, "Pf ff"

00:08:47.733 --> 00:08:50.320
everything is just, and I've
been saying this for years,

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.350
but it, you know any amount
of little success I have,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.207
I'm always like,

00:08:53.207 --> 00:08:55.110
"Okay everything else is
just a cherry on top."

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.500
'Cause we know so many
singers that are amazing,

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.020
amazing dancers, amazing
entertainers that never hit.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.780
And you don't know why or, you know

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.030
and everybody works hard.

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.860
So it's just like, I
always say everything is

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.680
like a cherry on top at this point.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.170
And then it's kind of a
beautiful way to live,

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.830
'cause it's how you just made your record.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:10.663
It's the cherry on top.

00:09:10.663 --> 00:09:11.530
You can do whatever you want

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.890
because it's your back to
that core thing of just like

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.940
why do you love music
and why you're writing,

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.490
and it's, it's lovely to talk to you.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.633
I love when you come on the show.

00:09:20.633 --> 00:09:23.280
- It's lovely to talk to you.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.113
- I love it.

00:09:24.113 --> 00:09:25.740
And I love, I love the cover too.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.990
Cause green is my favorite color.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.270
We have the same name and initial.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.130
I love it.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.570
All right, well Kelly's new EP

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.270
is called "K" and it's out now.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.537
You gotta check it out.

